	"summary": "2 findings, both fixed and each reproduced first as a failing test on the unchanged code; together they are the overlap of release run 40891943183 (two processes inside withLock at once). F1: judge called a lock that was gone abandoned (touched() gave 0), and takeOver then removed a fresh lock another waiter's mkdir had just made. F2: a waiter read the owner, the owner released and exited, another waiter made a fresh lock, and the waiter's kill(0) then condemned that fresh lock. With the fix (a gone lock is never abandoned; a dead pid counts only while owner.json still names that same holder) the three frozen properties hold for 2 and 3 waiters (1,062,013 states, depth 54, liveness included); 6 of 6 mutations are detected. On macOS the old code overlapped once in 16 x 200 rounds; the fixed code had no overlap in 16 x 400 and 16 x 1000.",
